  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "The following table gives the values of functions $g(x)$ and ${g}^{\u2032}(x)$ at some points. Find $({g}^{-1})^{\u2032}(2).$\n\n| **$x$** | $g(x)$ | ${g}^{\u2032}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $3$ | $-6$ |\n| $5$ | $2$ | $-5$ |\n| $7$ | $-2$ | $2$ |",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse is\n\n$$\n({g}^{-1})^{\u2032}(x)=\\frac{1}{{g}^{\u2032}({g}^{-1}(x))}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=2,$ we have\n\n$$\n({g}^{-1})^{\u2032}(2)=\\frac{1}{{g}^{\u2032}({g}^{-1}(2))}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we obtain ${g}^{-1}(2)=5$ and ${g}^{\u2032}(5)=-5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({g}^{-1})^{\u2032}(2) & =\\frac{1}{{g}^{\u2032}({g}^{-1}(2))} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{g}^{\u2032}(5)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(-5)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
